Infrastructure as Code (IaC) and Its Security
Learning Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Understand the fundamentals of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) and its security implications • Create and deploy infrastructure using Terraform templates • Implement security scanning for IaC templates using Terraform Validator and Checkov • Write and enforce security policies using Pulumi and Open Policy Agent (OPA) • Integrate security policy enforcement into CI/CD pipelines • Apply security best practices for cloud infrastructure automation

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of cloud computing concepts • Familiarity with command-line interface operations • Basic knowledge of YAML and JSON file formats • Understanding of version control systems (Git) • No prior experience with Terraform or Pulumi required

